---
name: "Cloudflare Logpush from S3 or R2 → OCSF → Hydrolix"
description: |
  Reads the HTTP request logs that a Logpush job writes to an S3-compatible
  bucket, such as Amazon S3 or Cloudflare R2, normalizes them to OCSF HTTP
  Activity, and writes them to a Hydrolix table.
---

let $url = "s3://example-logpush/http_requests/**/*.log.gz?region=us-east-1"

from_file $url, watch=true {
  decompress_gzip
  read_ndjson
}
cloudflare::ocsf::normalize dataset="http_requests"
to_hydrolix "https://hydrolix.example.com",
  table="security.ocsf",
  token=secret("HYDROLIX_TOKEN")
